# PenguScript manual declaration binding for the miniaudio audio library
# (miniaudio.h). miniaudio: https://github.com/mackron/miniaudio
# (public domain / MIT-0 at your choice). Vendored version 0.11.25.
#
# This is a declaration file (.d.pengu): it declares a small documented
# subset of the native C surface so the LSP and the semantic checker know
# the shape of miniaudio from PenguScript. The real C declarations live in
# `miniaudio.h`, which is `include`d below, so nothing here emits C code.
#
# Bound subset (deliberately tiny - everything that is meaningful WITHOUT an
# audio device or backend, plus the macros every program needs):
#   - version macros ........ MA_VERSION_MAJOR / MINOR / REVISION (0/11/25)
#   - ma_version_string() ... "0.11.25" (const char*, never NULL)
#   - ma_version(...) ....... writes major/minor/revision into three u32
#                             out-pointers
#
# INTENTIONALLY OMITTED (documented - the reason this binding is a curated
# subset and NOT a full binding):
#   - Every audio-backend API (ma_context*, ma_device*, ma_engine*,
#     ma_sound*, decoding, resampling, ring buffers, PCM converters, ...).
#     Those functions either need a real audio device/backend (unusable on a
#     headless host and in CI) or require caller-owned byte buffers that
#     PenguScript cannot yet express. The single-header implementation is
#     also NOT compiled into the Pengu runtime libraries (see
#     std_c/wrappers notes in build_runtime.py), so the declarations below
#     are documentation/type-checking only until a project supplies its own
#     `#define MINIAUDIO_IMPLEMENTATION` translation unit.
#
# Type mapping notes:
#   - ma_uint32 out-parameters are typed `ref to u32`; pass `sigil of` a
#     u32 variable.
#   - C `const char*` returns/receivers are typed `ref to frozen char` (the
#     read-only view; a PenguScript string literal converts to it directly).
#   - ma_result codes (MA_SUCCESS = 0, MA_ERROR = -1, MA_NO_BACKEND = -203,
#     ...) are C enum constants and are usable directly from PenguScript.
#
# Typical usage:
#   import std.miniaudio
#   var major as u32 is 0
#   var minor as u32 is 0
#   var rev as u32 is 0
#   calling miniaudio.ma_version with sigil of major, sigil of minor, sigil of rev
#
# Memory ownership follows the native library contract: none of the
# declarations below return an owned handle (only version queries are bound),
# so no release routine is required from PenguScript.
include "miniaudio.h"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Constants (semantic only; the real macros live in miniaudio.h)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

const MA_VERSION_MAJOR as i64 is 0
const MA_VERSION_MINOR as i64 is 11
const MA_VERSION_REVISION as i64 is 25

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Functions (real C symbol names used verbatim - no insignia)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

declare ma_version with pMajor as ref to u32, pMinor as ref to u32, pRevision as ref to u32 into void

declare ma_version_string into ref to frozen char
